{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And he said, גם עתה, etc.</b> One needs to understand his saying <b>גם</b> — what is newly introduced at this point regarding the judgment. And further, it is difficult, his saying <b>כדבריכם כן הוא</b> ('according to your words, so it is'), for it appears to me to be the opposite of their words: for they said ״אשר ימצא אתו ומת״ ('with whom it is found, he shall die'), and he said ״יהיה עבד״ ('he shall be a slave')." "Or perhaps he intended to respond to what they said, ״הן כסף אשר מצאנו״ ('behold, the silver we found'), etc., and he said: ״גם עתה — even now, after you have come under suspicion in this matter, I vindicate your words that you did not steal, and you stand in your original presumption of trustworthiness. But you cannot vindicate each and every one of you, for it is possible that among them there is a brother who acted without faithfulness, and it was he who took the goblet. And my claim is against only one of you, and his judgment is that he shall be a slave to me.״ And although he is liable to death, the matter is in my hand to enslave him until such time as I wish to put him to death." "<b>Or</b> it may intend that he argued that there is no soundness in their mouths when they said ״ומת,״ for the death penalty applies only if there is testimony concerning the theft — that they saw him take it. But finding it in his possession is only circumstantial inference (אומדנא); he would be liable only under civil law (דינא דמלכותא)." "And his saying <b>ואתם תהיו נקיים</b> ('and you shall be clear') — for they stand in the presumption of fitness, and they are not caught under the law of a group of ten when stolen property is found in the hand of one of them, since there is no testimony against them that they conspired together and stole."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:33.875870478Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}